# HANASO web — environment variable NAMES (non-secret samples only).
# Real values never live in git. Local dev needs none of these — without DATABASE_URL
# the app runs on the in-memory DEV-ONLY repositories (exactly like before M0-10).

# Non-secret, safe to expose to the client:
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENV=local
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=dev
NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_SHA=dev

# --- M0-10 database layer ---
# Set DATABASE_URL to switch the repositories onto PostgreSQL 18 (app + /api/ready).
# Production points at PgBouncer (transaction mode, scram); local dev can point
# straight at a postgres instance. Integration tests use TEST_DATABASE_URL instead.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://hanaso:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/hanaso
# Direct (non-PgBouncer) URL — migrations/seed/backup/restore only (falls back to DATABASE_URL):
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://hanaso:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/hanaso
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://hanaso:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/postgres
# DB_POOL_MAX=8

# --- M1 (auth) — see db/schema/auth.ts + modules/auth (AUTH-ACCOUNTS 2026-11-24) ---
# The account session machinery (sessions, mnemonic sealing, lookup keys,
# oauth cookie) derives from HANASO_SESSION_SECRET — no extra secret needed.
# Four login methods:
#   mnemonic — always available (no env)
#   email    — needs the transport block below
#   google   — needs GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET
#   sms      — infrastructure only («به‌زودی») — SMS_* variables are future use

# --- email login transport (one of: none | resend | smtp) ---
# none (default): /api/auth/email/* answers 503 honestly — no fake login.
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=none
# resend (pure HTTPS, zero deps):
# RESEND_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# smtp (nodemailer; port 465 = implicit TLS, 587 = STARTTLS):
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=CHANGE_ME
# sender identity for both transports:
# EMAIL_FROM=HANASO <no-reply@CHANGE_ME>

# --- google login (Authorization Code + PKCE) ---
# From Google Cloud Console → OAuth client (Web application), with the exact
# redirect URI https://<your-domain>/api/auth/google/callback registered.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=CHANGE_ME.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME

# --- SMS login (future activation — currently infrastructure-only) ---
# SMS_TRANSPORT=
# SMS_API_KEY=
# SMS_SENDER_NUMBER=

# --- TASK-HANASO-24: session tokens (signed hanaso_lid) ---
# REQUIRED in production (the app refuses to boot without it). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# HANASO_SESSION_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_64_HEX_CHARS
# Bounds the pre-24 raw-cookie -> signed-token re-issue grace. Recommended at
# deploy time: NOW + 14 days (existing learners keep their progress linked;
# after the date raw values are never re-signed — fail-closed). ISO-8601:
# HANASO_LEGACY_TOKEN_CUTOFF=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z

# ─── Temporary Preview Mode (owner review pass — FINALIZATION) ───
# Unset = the feature is completely inert (every /preview/* route 404s).
# Set (a long random hex string) to let the OWNER browse drafts/unpublished
# chapters with locks bypassed. The value is server-only; the cookie stores
# only an HMAC of it. See src/lib/preview.ts. Never reuse the session secret.
# PREVIEW_MODE_KEY=
